messages:
ida: Quick heads-up — users hitting the new Next + LangChain starter (edge-ready) reported flaky 401s in staging. Locally fine.

tom: Can you share the edge handler? Edge vs node differences matter.

ida: Handler is tiny (Next edge route):
```js
import { createClient } from 'redwood-sdk'
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY })
export default async function handler(req) {
  const { prompt } = await req.json()
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(await client.generate({ model: 'gpt-lite', prompt })))
}
```
No explicit refresh. Deployed preview shows ~1% 401s during a 1000-request spike and the SDK doesn't retry.

nora: Sounds like the refresh singleflight race in non-node runtimes. We implemented a mutex in node but not a web-safe Promise singleflight. Multiple inflight requests race to refresh and some go out with expired token.

ida: Short-term mitigation: add an opt-in RW_EDGE_RETRY flag in the starter and a tiny retry wrapper in the template README. Not enabled by default. Example snippet in README: ```js
async function safeGenerate(client, opts){
  for(let i=0;i<2;i++){
    try { return await client.generate(opts) } catch(e){
      if (e.status === 401 && process.env.RW_EDGE_RETRY==='true') await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, 120*(i+1))); else throw e
    }
  }
  throw new Error('retries exhausted')
}
```

tom: Long-term SDK plan: add a web/edge-safe singleflight (Promise-based) so only one refresh runs and inflight callers wait, then auto-retry. Also add clearer errors when refresh egress is blocked. I'll file an issue: js-sdk:edge-singleflight and add an edge-emulator test that blocks the refresh endpoint and fires 50 concurrent requests.

nora: Also we saw a related embed serialization mismatch between the JS sample and Python eval harness (1D vs 2D). Quick fix in sample: always send embeddings as list-of-lists; on python side coerce with np.atleast_2d. Add note in README.

ida: I pushed a tiny PR with the opt-in retry + README notes and a CI spike test (node edge-emulator) behind a feature flag. Will link the SDK issue in the PR.

sdk-bot: Issue created: js-sdk/1350 "edge singleflight + inflight retry" assigned to eng-devex.

tom: Once SDK patch lands we should remove the sample wrapper and update the README. Also add an e2e in SDK repo that ensures <0.5% 401s on a 500-request spike in emulator.

ida: Thanks — ping me if you want to review the README wording. :sparkles:
